       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults. The usual prescription maximum is 3,200 mg/day, and single doses are generally capped at 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWas this a typo or a mix-up? These are some common regimens:\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a typical anti-inflammatory dose\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours**, for analgesia\n\nIf you really do want 1600 mg per dose, I can enter it with a note documenting the rationale. Please confirm the dose and frequency you want. I'll enter whichever order you choose."
